## 1. The law (put this, abbreviated, in the project contract)

Every data source, present or future, climbs this ladder in order. No agent
skips a rung; exceptions are owner decisions recorded in `DECISIONS.md`.

1. **Free and open first.** A zero-cost, commercially-compatible public source
   is always preferred, even at lower resolution/cadence. Licence verified
   BEFORE ingestion — name, verification date, evidence URL — in the project's
   data-source registry.
2. **Commercial/NC alternatives are CATALOGued, never silently ingested.**
   A better source with a blocking licence becomes a catalog entry
   (tier: upgrade) with its licence, cost note, and an honest one-line
   "unlocks". Activation is a per-customer flag; a flag with no built
   ingestion must say so ("flag only — ingestion not yet built").
3. **Unclear licences get a NEGOTIATION state, not a guess.** Write to the
   provider; track `contacted → agreed → contracted` with dates in the
   catalog. Unclear = unusable until answered.
4. **NC-blocked can be REBUILT.** Where a blocking licence stops a feature,
   the preferred answer is a reproducible build of an equivalent-or-better
   dataset from licence-clean open inputs — a branded first-party dataset,
   registered, priceable, optionally exposed via API.

**The test:** *"Could a paying customer, an auditor, and the data provider all
read our catalog entry for this source and find it exactly true?"* If not, the
entry — or the ingestion — is wrong.

---

## 2. The catalog (machine-readable, admin-visible)

One entry per source that is in use, upgradable, under negotiation, or ours.
Suggested shape (adapt to your stack; keep every field honest):

```
{ id, category, name,
  tier: "in-use-free" | "upgrade-commercial" | "upgrade-nc-blocked"
      | "negotiation" | "proprietary",
  licence, licence_verified, evidence_url,
  replaces,            // the in-use source this would upgrade
  unlocks,             // ONE honest line: what feature/quality it enables
  cost_note,           // verified price or "UNVERIFIED — no quote"
  negotiation: { status, contacted, note },        // tier=negotiation
  build_script,        // tier=proprietary: pointer to the reproducible runner
  output_licence,      // tier=proprietary: OUR choice, or inherited (e.g. ODbL share-alike)
  api_exposed, pricing_note,
  activation: { per-customer flags }               // flags only where ingestion exists
}
```

Surface it in the admin console as three sections: **Upgrades** (with
activation toggles), **Negotiations** (editable status/date/note), and
**First-party datasets** (build script, output licence, cost, price, API).

